# Vauxhall Carlton Mk1 saloon, 1978-1986.
#
# The first Carlton: the rear-wheel-drive replacement for the Victor, sold
# from September 1978 with the 1.8 and 2.0 fours and the 2.8 six, and built
# in Luton and at Russelsheim. The saloon is modelled; the estate is not
# separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_Carlton
#
# Dimensions 4.620 x 1.725 x 1.470 m, wheelbase 2.668 m. A period road test
# gives 4.742 x 1.775 x 1.361 m; the conflict is recorded rather than
# averaged, and the infobox figures are modelled.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is near-level, about 5-8 degrees behind the
# centre, so the flank is a close estimate and the limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no Vauxhall colour list was read. White, Red, Blue and
# Silver are plain names. Bright Copper Metallic is the only name found, from
# an insurers listing, and is not used. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 180 km/h. Comfort 65/280, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 65. Classes 1,2.
# Dates: intro September 1978; retires staggered 1994-1997 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-carlton-mk1.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-carlton-mk1.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-carlton-mk1/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the late-1982-on facelift saloon represents the
# 1978-86 generation, the earlier grille-less nose not being represented. The
# published dimensions are used rather than the conflicting road-test figures,
# and the side stations are estimated from a slightly rearward view.


obj=citycar
name=VauxhallCarltonMk1(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=1978
intro_month=9
retire_year=1997
retire_month=6
speed=180
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=65
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=280

